delta-change "typed-holes-diagnostics"
message "TypedHoleDiagnostics: typed holes bounded parse recovery and source diagnostics"
author "ai"
doc "guide" """
  |# TypedHoleDiagnostics: typed holes, bounded recovery, and diagnostics
  |
  |TypedHoleDiagnostics is a post-constitution product delta layered over StatementSuites. It does
  |not modify the frozen F0-F11 bootstrap constitution.
  |
  |## Purpose
  |
  |StatementSuites gives Trellis a fully graph-defined, recursively nestable offside
  |syntax. TypedHoleDiagnostics adds the minimum front-end structure needed for incomplete
  |source and interactive editing without weakening the ordinary compiler parser.
  |
  |The central distinction is:
  |
  |```text
  |strict parse     invalid source -> failure
  |recovering parse invalid source -> graph-authorized edit -> typed AST + diagnostic
  |```
  |
  |Strict parsing remains fail-closed.
  |
  |## Typed holes
  |
  |A hole is a first-class grammar expression rather than a special parser return
  |value:
  |
  |```text
  |grammar.hole
  |  surface = "?"
  |  sort    -> Expr
  |```
  |
  |Bool0 adds the ordinary constructor `language.bool0.ctor.Hole : Expr` and a
  |normal atom production whose body is the hole expression. Therefore `?` is
  |valid explicit incomplete syntax and prints canonically as `?`.
  |
  |Because hole surface text is graph data, changing `?` to `??` through the free
  |change language changes both strict parsing and recovery insertion without host
  |parser changes.
  |
  |## Recovery policy
  |
  |`grammar.bool0.recovery` selects a bounded strategy graph:
  |
  |```text
  |max-edits            = 1
  |selection            = unique-edit
  |candidate-boundaries = real-token-ends
  |failure               = strict
  |strategy01            -> grammar.recovery.strategy.insert-hole
  |hole                  -> grammar.bool0.g11.hole.body
  |```
  |
  |The TypedHoleDiagnostics recovery API first runs the normal strict parser. Only after that
  |fails may it try the selected recovery strategy. A recovery result is accepted
  |only when exactly one authorized edit yields a complete tree.
  |
  |TypedHoleDiagnostics deliberately does not add arbitrary token deletion, insertion of
  |ordinary syntax, or error productions. Those can be later recovery strategies
  |if they can be made equally explicit and bounded.
  |
  |## Diagnostics
  |
  |Recovery produces a stable graph-selected diagnostic:
  |
  |```text
  |severity -> diagnostic.severity.error
  |code     -> diagnostic.code.inserted-hole
  |offsets  = UTF-8 bytes
  |expected = sort-name
  |```
  |
  |A recovered `true&&` therefore has a zero-width diagnostic span at byte 6 and
  |an expected item of `Expr`.
  |
  |For Unicode source such as `π&&`, the insertion span is `[4,4)`, because `π`
  |occupies two UTF-8 bytes.
  |
  |## Recovery result
  |
  |The host exposes the graph interpretation as:
  |
  |```scala
  |RecoveredParse(
  |  tree: Tree,
  |  diagnostics: Vector[ParseDiagnostic],
  |  edits: Vector[RecoveryEdit]
  |)
  |```
  |
  |For valid source, `parseRecovering` returns the exact strict tree and empty
  |`diagnostics`/`edits`.
  |
  |For incomplete source:
  |
  |```text
  |source:    true&&
  |strict:    failure
  |recovered: true && ?
  |```
  |
  |The tree is an ordinary `And(True, Hole)` tree. The hole is not an out-of-band
  |marker.
  |
  |## Layout composition
  |
  |Recovery candidates are inserted into source and then passed through the same
  |StatementSuites lexer, layout generator, and suite parser. This makes recovery compose
  |with nested suites without a separate layout recovery path. For example:
  |
  |```text
  |block
  |  true
  |  !
  |```
  |
  |can recover to a block whose second item is `Not(Hole)`.
  |
  |## Invariants
  |
  |TypedHoleDiagnostics tests enforce:
  |
  |1. canonical StatementSuites + TypedHoleDiagnostics.delta derivation,
  |2. first-class hole/recovery/diagnostic vocabulary,
  |3. explicit holes parse under the strict parser,
  |4. incomplete infix recovery inserts one typed hole,
  |5. diagnostics use UTF-8 byte offsets,
  |6. recovery composes with recursive layout suites,
  |7. complete StatementSuites programs remain observationally identical,
  |8. DeltaBool0 can evolve the hole surface,
  |9. invalid recovery policy edits fail closed,
  |10. TypedHoleDiagnostics remains outside F0-F11 and all earlier product identities.
  |
  """
test "canonical delta contract"
  assert "canonical"
  assert "valid"
  assert "source-roundtrip"
  assert "dependency" "statements-suites"
  assert "introduces" "grammar.component.hole" "grammar.component"
depends "statements-suites"
  entity "grammar.component.hole" "grammar.component"
    port "self" "out" "3:cap4:meta12:unrestricted14:4:atom6:Schema6:4:none"
    attr "description" "explicit incomplete syntax represented as an ordinary typed grammar expression"
    attr "name" "Hole"
    attr "slice" "TypedHoleDiagnostics"
  entity "grammar.component.recovery" "grammar.component"
    port "self" "out" "3:cap4:meta12:unrestricted14:4:atom6:Schema6:4:none"
    attr "description" "declares bounded graph-selected parse recovery strategies"
    attr "name" "Recovery"
